The '''Energia Tèrmica de l'Estat de Balboa''' (ETEB) is a [[state-owned enterprise]] responsible for thermal power generation in [[Balboa]]. The company operates natural gas-fired and petroleum-fired power plants, supplying approximately 22 per cent of Balboa's electricity combined. ETEB's role has been declining as nuclear and renewable capacity has expanded under the [[1996 Adonian Community Edict on a Green Transition for the New Millennium]].

== History ==

=== Formation (1974) ===

ETEB was established in 1974, shortly after reunification, to consolidate the petroleum-fired power plants that had been built to support the canal corridor economy and the [[Badia Curta]] industrial complex. The company was created under the Ministry of Energy and Natural Resources to manage thermal generation as a complement to hydropower, particularly during dry seasons when hydroelectric output declined.

=== Natural gas expansion ===

In the 1980s and 1990s, ETEB expanded into natural gas-fired generation, using a mix of imported gas and gas supplied by [[CIEA]] from its refining operations at Badia Curta. Natural gas plants were cleaner and more efficient than the older oil-fired units, and their construction reflected the government's efforts to reduce urban air pollution in the canal corridor and the Sant Cristòfor metropolitan area.

=== Decline ===

The establishment of the [[Organització d'Energia Nuclear de Balboa|OENB]] and the commissioning of the [[Central Nuclear de Sant Feliu]] in 2010 marked the beginning of a planned reduction in ETEB's role. Nuclear power provided stable baseload electricity without the air pollution associated with thermal generation, and the government's policy has been to gradually reduce petroleum-fired generation in particular. Natural gas-fired generation remains part of the mix, as it produces lower emissions than oil-fired plants and benefits from a combination of imported supply and CIEA's domestic gas.

== Operations ==

* '''Headquarters''': [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]
* '''Natural gas share''': approximately 14% of Balboa's electricity (2026)
* '''Petroleum/oil share''': approximately 8% of Balboa's electricity (2026)
* '''Employees''': approximately 2,400 (2026)

ETEB operates a number of thermal power plants across Balboa, with the largest facilities located near the Badia Curta industrial complex and the canal corridor. Natural gas is supplied through a mix of imports and gas from [[CIEA]]'s refining operations, while petroleum for oil-fired generation is sourced from domestic offshore production ([[Corporació Petrolífera de l'Estat de Balboa|CPEB]]) and imported crude.

== Ownership ==

ETEB is wholly owned by the [[Government of Balboa]]. It operates under the oversight of the Ministry of Energy and Natural Resources and is not listed on any stock exchange.

